    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Kyle Tucker** (77.20) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) anchor our lineup as the premier starts. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against Marte, whose 5.16 xERA suggests significant room for damage, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives in a high-leverage spot hitting third against Pfaadt, where the dynamic platoon advantage provides a +14% boost to his output. **Coby Mayo** (66.72) also stands out; although facing Gasser, his park factor (+16%) and the high probability of stolen base opportunities against a slow-delivering pitcher make him a vital asset in our pursuit of speed. We are leaning heavily on these core bats to sustain our category production, particularly as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.56) provides a high-floor presence in the two-hole against Quantrill.\n\nThe bench decision process was most difficult regarding **Nasim Nunez** (54.17). He nearly cracked the lineup based on his profile as a speed-first utility option, but he ultimately fell short of the threshold compared to the high-efficiency projected production of **Sam Antonacci** and **Henry Bolte**. While **Sam Antonacci** and **Henry Bolte** hold lower raw ceilings, their lineup positioning at the top of the order ensures enough plate appearances to mitigate the risk of falling behind in our daily efficiency targets. We are keeping a close eye on the weather and potential late-scratches, though all confirmed lineups are currently favorable. **Brayan Rocchio** (54.65) remains the most volatile play today; while his SP skill score is robust at +19%, the -8% penalty from the number nine spot in the order keeps his ceiling capped. We will continue to monitor the performance of **Josh Jung** (54.98), who is currently riding the line between a marginal start and a must-start, requiring a strong showing against Soriano to justify his placement.",
